 -tests were used to derive p-values, and p<0.05 was considered statistically significant.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"The anomaly detection method is automated to alternate between adaptive multiple linear regression and exponentially weighted moving average (EWMA) based on baseline data.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Calculated as the percentage with no age stratification for each HHS region during the exposure days\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}